{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.FigureEightReebRotation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.FigureEightReebRotation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Norm","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.unit_modulus_of_det_one_small_trace"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figureEightTrace_golden","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figureEightTrace_golden","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/figure-eight-reeb-rotation.lean#L102-L112","doc":"**`θ = 0` at the golden ratio.** If `q² = q + 1` (the golden relation, `q = φ`)\nthen `tr M_{4₁}(q) = 2`, so the Reeb eigenvalue is `+1` (`θ = 0`): the operator\ndegenerates exactly at the `A`-polynomial complex-volume branch point\n`u = 2 ln φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figureEightTrace_sub_two_factored","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figureEightTrace_sub_two_factored","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/figure-eight-reeb-rotation.lean#L92-L100","doc":"**`tr M − 2` factors; the golden root is `q² − q − 1`.** The four factors are\n`(q²−q−1)(q²+q−1)` (the golden pair, real roots `q = φ`, `1/φ` up to sign) and\n`(q²−q+1)(q²+q+1) = Φ₆(q)Φ₆(−q)` (the cusp/cyclotomic pair, no real roots). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figureEightTrace_ge_neg_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figureEightTrace_ge_neg_two","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/figure-eight-reeb-rotation.lean#L85-L90","doc":"`tr M_{4₁}(q) ≥ −2` on the real axis (`θ ≤ π`, never a full flip). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figureEightTrace_add_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figureEightTrace_add_two","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/figure-eight-reeb-rotation.lean#L76-L83","doc":"**`tr M + 2` is a perfect square.** Hence `tr M_{4₁}(q) ≥ −2` for every real\n`q ≠ 0`: the Reeb rotation never reaches `θ = π` on the real substrate axis\n(it does so only at the complex cusp shape `q² = e^{iπ/3}`, where the square's\nbase `q² − 1 + q⁻²` — i.e. `q⁴ − q² + 1 = Φ₆(q²)` — vanishes). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figureEightTrace_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figureEightTrace_one","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/figure-eight-reeb-rotation.lean#L59-L63","doc":"**Classical trace value.** `tr M_{4₁}|_{q=1} = −1`: at `q = 1` the seminormal\nblock is the `S₃` representation and `(σ₁σ₂)²` is a 3-cycle. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figureEightTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figureEightTrace","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/figure-eight-reeb-rotation.lean#L53-L57","doc":"Closed-form trace of `M_{4₁} = (σ₁σ₂⁻¹)²` on `V_(2,1)` as a Laurent polynomial\nin `q` (from the explicit seminormal block). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figure_eight_unitary_on_standard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figure_eight_unitary_on_standard","kind":"theorem","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/figure-eight-reeb-rotation.lean#L25-L39","doc":"**Figure-eight knot operator is unitary on `V_(2,1)`.**\n\nThe knot operator `M_{4₁} = (σ₁σ₂⁻¹)²` has determinant `1` (product of\nfour generator determinants, each `-1`), and its trace `t` on `V_(2,1)`\nis real with `t² < 4`; hence by `unit_modulus_of_det_one_small_trace`\nits eigenvalues have unit modulus `‖λ‖ = 1`.  This is the precise\nstatement of the md proposition (replacing the prior placeholder\n`(-1)^4 = 1 ∧ 2 = 2`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:figure-eight-reeb-rotation","label":"prop:figure-eight-reeb-rotation","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/figure-eight-reeb-rotation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figure_eight_det_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.figure_eight_det_one","kind":"theorem","line":20,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/figure-eight-reeb-rotation.lean#L20-L23","doc":"The determinant of the figure-eight knot operator\nM_{4₁} = (σ₁σ₂⁻¹)² on a 2-dim representation is 1.\ndet(σ₁) = −1, det(σ₂⁻¹) = −1, so det(M) = (−1)⁴ = 1. ","signatureChunk":0}]}